<title>SRI LANKA: Tea Smallholder dips on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Tea Smallholder dips on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tea Smallholder Factories Ltd fell nine percent, or 1.75 rupees to 17.50 on turnover of 3,200 shares in profit-taking by small investors, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Small retail investors are booking profits, since the share gained sharply in the past 10 days,&quot; said a broker specialising in retail clientele.  </p>
<p>Investors have been bullish on plantation shares and allied scrips since Sri Lankan tea prices have been at near record highs in 1996.</p>
<p>The company processes tea bought from small cultivators.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
